Southeastern Athletic Conference
The Southeastern Athletic Conference (known as the South Atlantic Intercollegiate Athletic Association between 1929 and 1942) was an intercollegiate athletic conference of HBCU's that existed from 1929 to 1961. The conference's members were located in Florida, Georgia, and South Carolina.

